entity spec_file                  # one .edda file under specs/
  path
  entity_name, optional           # the entity its first entity line declares
  stories: many story
  notes: many note
  may create: agent
  may read:   agent, operator
  may update: agent
  may delete: nobody

entity note, part of spec_file    # one note: line, wherever it sits
  text
  story_id, optional

story the checker refuses what it cannot read               # EDDA-001
  as an agent
  i want every sentence that is not in the grammar refused with its line
  so that a file that passes has one reading and nothing hidden in it
  epic: CHK
  tags: checker, level-1

  operation check(file) returns
    [problem for problem in file's problems]
    who: agent, operator

  example an unknown keyword is refused
    given spec_file bad with path "fixtures/unknown_keyword.edda"
    when  agent asks check(bad)
    then  done
          count(check(bad)) is 1
          check(bad)[0]'s kind is refused
          check(bad)[0]'s line is 3
          check(bad)[0]'s message is "unknown keyword: ensures"

  example an unknown name is refused
    given spec_file bad with path "fixtures/unknown_name.edda"
    when  agent asks check(bad)
    then  done
          check(bad)[0]'s kind is refused
          check(bad)[0]'s message is "unknown name: units_sold"

  example a tab is refused
    given spec_file bad with path "fixtures/tab.edda"
    when  agent asks check(bad)
    then  done
          check(bad)[0]'s message is "a tab; use two spaces"

  example a step at level 1 is refused
    given spec_file bad with path "fixtures/step_at_level_1.edda"
    when  agent asks check(bad)
    then  done
          check(bad)[0]'s message is "a step at level 1: set the order's status"

  example returns and ensure on one operation is refused
    given spec_file bad with path "fixtures/returns_and_ensure.edda"
    when  agent asks check(bad)
    then  done
          check(bad)[0]'s message is "returns and ensure on one operation: open_orders"

  example a status not in its list is refused
    given spec_file bad with path "fixtures/unknown_status.edda"
    when  agent asks check(bad)
    then  done
          check(bad)[0]'s message is "status not in its list: archived"

  example a story in the wrong file is refused
    given spec_file bad with path "fixtures/wrong_file.edda"
    when  agent asks check(bad)
    then  done
          check(bad)[0]'s message is "story FUL-005 belongs in order.edda"

  example a clean file has no problems
    given spec_file good with path "fixtures/order.edda"
    when  agent asks check(good)
    then  done
          check(good) is []

story the checker flags what is allowed but doubtful              # EDDA-002
  as a operator
  i want unreachable statuses, stories without an example and open
    questions on done stories shown as flags, not refusals
  so that the file still passes and I can decide what to do
  epic: CHK
  tags: checker, level-1

  example a status nothing reaches is flagged
    given spec_file odd with path "fixtures/unreachable_status.edda"
    when  agent asks check(odd)
    then  done
          check(odd)[0]'s kind is flagged
          check(odd)[0]'s message is "no change reaches status: archived"

  example a story with no example is flagged
    given spec_file odd with path "fixtures/no_example.edda"
    when  agent asks check(odd)
    then  done
          check(odd)[0]'s kind is flagged
          check(odd)[0]'s message is "story FUL-009 has no example"

story every note is collected in one place                          # EDDA-003
  as a operator
  i want every note: line across all files listed together, grouped by
    wording
  so that a kind of note that keeps coming back shows itself
  epic: CHK
  tags: checker, backlog
  question: should two notes with the same words but different stories
    count as one kind or two?

  operation notes(files) returns
    [note for file in files for note in file's notes]
    who: agent, operator

  example notes from two files are listed together
    given spec_file a with path "fixtures/notes_a.edda"
          spec_file b with path "fixtures/notes_b.edda"
    when  operator asks notes([a, b])
    then  done
          count(notes([a, b])) is 3
          notes([a, b])[0]'s text is "the stock feed is refreshed every night"
